aranta@milton.u.washington.edu (Aaron Ranta) writes:

>Since people tend to put in future nethack suggestions here, I've
>created a list of some things I'd like to see in Nethack in future version(s)...

>- Make it so you can no longer wish for the more powerful artifacts.
>  (ie: Mjollnir, Excalibur, Stormbringer ).  Maybe give you a ordinary
>  war hammer/longsword/broad sword.  You should only be able to attain
>  these items through the normal channels (ie:sacrifice).
>  Perhaps make these guys have a 'personality'...

Disagree. It's much harder to get a wish then to get something through
sacrifice. With a blessed luckstone and suitable items to create monster,
you can get Excalibur, Stormbringer, and all sort of minor artifacts easily.
I would rather limit the chance to get artifact through sacrifice then
restriction of getting them through wishes...

>- add some class specific items to the dungeon that only a certain class
>  can use  (ie: holy items for priest, thiefly tools for rogues, magical
>  paraphernelia for the wizards, et al, just so much dead weight for
>  those none in the appropriate class(es) )

Disagree again. Current scene that some classes of character will uses
some tools more effectively seems to be sufficienct. Why can a rogue
be talented in using magical items???

>- more character classes! (one per letter would be fun)
>  I especially liked the demon class mentioned a while back (from lowly
>  manes to mighty demon prince!)

Yes, yes, yes...

>- a new special water level.  Perhaps a large underground lake?
>  Would allow the addition of many aquatic-type baddies (sea dragons,
>  kraken,mermen/maids,syrens,sharks, et al)

No need for this. If the Dev. team make the level compiler code works
and able to load special levels at run time, then every game adminstrator
can create their own special levels. I would prefer they expand this
idea a little bit more to have a dungeon compiler -- i.e.
one who can specify the probabilites where you place the special levels,
the probabilites where you put a shop, or graveyard, blah, blah, blah
on runtime through a configuration file.

>  Add two new intrinsics: swim - allow person to cross over water
>  squares (great for pools!) but acts much like levitation in that you
>  can not pick up anything in the water on the bottom as you are
>  swimming along the surface...

Agree, but I would prefer a small variation of this intrinsics: If
someone has the swin intrinsics, he/she can cross over water without any
danger under normal condition. If he/she is weak or confusing or 
hallucination, etc. He/She has a small chance to drown. If the player
doesn't have this intrinsics, he/she will have a big chance to drown
(the chance should depend on his/hers luck) Perhaps a player with bad luck
should always drown ;-)

>just some thoughts.... (comments?)

Another thing I want is some truely magical artifact. Currently, the
Excalibur, Stormbringer, etc are too easy to get and too lame as a weapon.
Make them harder to get and more powerful and has more interesting side
effect. e.g:

for Mjollnir:

	you can't weild it unless you have gaunlet of power.

for Stormbringer:

	If you weild it for a long time without killing anything, 
	Stormbringer will get bored and try to attack you instead ;-)

a long sword named Sikanda (ref: NeverEnding Story)

	If you doesn't fullfil certain conditions before you try to
	touch it, you die. If you are in danger, it will jump to your
	hand and give you 4 and 5 strokes in each round. If you weild
	it by your own will, it will bring you bad luck.

a Scythe named Death:

	should always be cursed, always has enchantment +66 or -66. If you
	try to enchant it or disenchant it, it won't work or it will simply
	be vaporized. You can never get to endgame will you are weilding it.
	
	   You try to climb up the ladder, oops, some mysterious force
	   pull you back to the realm of death....


In general, the more powerful the item, the more difficult to get it...

Just some other suggestions..			-achille

	



